  "note": "Triennial town commissioners election of May 1949. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1950 lists the commissioners (eight names for nine seats). Eight names printed for nine seats (the ninth is not named: vacancy or omission). Robert Elliott and William M'Cready follow a semicolon, but an R. Elliott and a W. M'Creedy were commissioners elected in 1946, so they are taken as commissioners, not officials. Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
